{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPDGk9hV1Uo1V916VqQhYV","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\n[paper.sh] reference query plan ready: 10 queries\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 1/10 | random walks universal traversal sequences complexity of maze problems\n[semantic_scholar] search failed | query 1/10 | random walks universal traversal sequences complexity of maze problems | Semantic Scholar HTTP 429 for https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/search?query=random+walks+universal+traversal+sequences+complexity+of+maze+problems&limit=25&fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 2/10 | tight upper bound on the cover time for random walks on graphs\n[semantic_scholar] search failed | query 2/10 | tight upper bound on the cover time for random walks on graphs | Semantic Scholar HTTP 429 for https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/search?query=tight+upper+bound+on+the+cover+time+for+random+walks+on+graphs&limit=25&fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 3/10 | Matthews covering problems for Markov chains hitting time bound\n[semantic_scholar] search complete | [------------] | refs 0/3 (3 left) | candidates 0/0 | query 3/10\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 4/10 | Lovasz random walks on graphs survey\n[semantic_scholar] search complete | [------------] | refs 0/3 (3 left) | candidates 0/25 | query 4/10\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [####--------] | refs 1/3 (2 left) | candidates 1/25 | query 4/10\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [########----] | refs 2/3 (1 left) | candidates 2/25 | query 4/10\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [############] | refs 3/3 (0 left) | candidates 3/25 | query 4/10\n[paper.sh] attempting scholarly fallback: OpenAlex fallback did not produce references\n[paper.sh] downstream fallbacks unavailable; using Semantic Scholar references","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75e1d124-5f7f-4219-805b-1d4a5db7e7d1","uuid":"a0882930-8e61-4972-b674-e38367ed16e4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:30:18.936Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `schol