{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wv8TazMRn3beHbv867j3o7","type":"tool_result","content":"139:Random tree & uniform labelled tree (Pr\\\"ufer) & 16 & 16 \\\\\n330:The evaluator (\\texttt{task/evaluate\\_final.py}) generates deterministic families from a public catalogue (\\texttt{det\\_catalogue}), with pool membership fixed by $n \\bmod 3$. Random families come from \\texttt{random\\_graph}: random trees from uniform Pr\\\"ufer sequences; Erd\\H{o}s--R\\'enyi graphs with $n$ uniform on $\\{5,\\dots,30\\}$, $p$ uniform on $[2\\ln n/n, \\max(0.5, 2\\ln n/n)]$, rejected until connected; random 3-regular graphs via a configuration model with even $n\\in\\{6,\\dots,30\\}$, rejected until simple and connected. Labels come from \\texttt{simulate\\_cover\\_times} with 256 walks per graph. Bootstrap intervals use 1000 replicates of the two-level scheme in \\S\\ref{sec:protocol}. \nOutput written on /agent-tmp/build/paper.pdf (12 pages, 325964 bytes).\nValidated 23 grounded claims and 5 provenance references.\nValidated sections and 4 citation key references.\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75e1d124-5f7f-4219-805b-1d4a5db7e7d1","uuid":"d19b137e-f2cf-44b5-9d18-d5cc96e86189","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:41:20.147Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"139:Random tree & uniform labelled tree (Pr\\\"ufer) & 16 & 16 \\\\\n330:The evaluator (\\texttt{task/evaluate\\_final.py}) generates deterministic families from a public catalogue (\\texttt{det\\_catalogue}), with pool membership fixed by $n \\bmod 3$. Random families come from \\texttt{random\\_graph}: random trees from uniform Pr\\\"ufer sequences; Erd\\H{o}s--R\\'enyi graphs with $n$ uniform on $\\{5,\\dots,30\\}$, $p$ uniform on $[2\\ln n/n, \\max(0.5, 2\\ln n/n)]$, rejected until connected; random 3-regular graphs via a configuration model with even $n\\in\\{6,\\dots,30\\}$, rejected until simple and connected. Labels come from \\texttt{simulate\\_cover\\_times} with 256 walks per graph. Bootstrap intervals use 1000 replicates of the two-level scheme in \\S\\ref{sec:protocol}. \nOutput written on /agent-tmp/build/paper.pdf (12 pages, 325964 bytes).\nValidated 23 grounded claims and 5 provenance references.\nValidated sections and 4 citation key references.\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evalu